# The count IS the exit status: tests/data/lector_intra.bin is 41 bytes, so
# `expect-exit=41` is the whole assertion. Nothing is written, so check_run's
# "wrote to stdout, expected nothing" is the second half of it -- a reader
# that stopped at the first 0x00 would exit 1, one that never saw EOF would
# be killed by the 20-second limit, and both are failures here.
#
# No stdout= and no expected.out: a program whose only output is its status.
TEST: expect-exit=41 stdin=tests/data/lector_intra.bin
